/* ORBIT Mega 2560 — SOFTWARE I2C: SDA=A4, SCL=A5.
   Move shared SDA from D20 to A4 and shared SCL from D21 to A5.
   Required libraries: U8g2, SoftwareWire (Testato), Adafruit BMP280 Library
   (install its Adafruit BusIO and Adafruit Unified Sensor dependencies).
   BMP280 ONLY: hardware I2C SDA=D20, SCL=D21; auto-detect 0x77 / 0x76.
   Keep the OLEDs and all existing software-I2C devices on A4/A5.
   D23 open: LCD temperature / humidity. Closed to GND: altitude / pressure.
   Altitude is estimated in feet using SEA_LEVEL_HPA below; pressure is hPa.
   Set SEA_LEVEL_HPA to local sea-level pressure (QNH) for calibrated altitude.
   BMP280 is local to the Mega; existing Uno UART protocol stays compatible.
   LCD=0x27, small OLED=0x3C, large OLED=0x3D, AHT30=0x38, INA219=0x40.
   INA219: assumes battery-side measurement and standard R100 shunt.
   One Fitinoch 12V 5Ah LiFePO4 battery; second pack is a spare.
   Percentage is a rough voltage estimate, NOT a calibrated fuel gauge.
   Usage totals reset at startup.
   RGB common cathode by default. EEPROM bytes 0..7 and 16..19 reserved.
   Sound settings: independent startup and air-sample tune, global mute.
   Home: strongest RAW AS7341 band; location/day-night are uncertain guesses.
   Debugging: tap D24 through information pages; hold Go back to return.
   Controls: D6 -> GND starts air sampling (dedicated button).
   D24 -> GND controls OLED: hold 2 seconds opens/selects; tap advances.
   D23 -> GND LCD switch; debounced state sent on UART1 AND UART3, 9600 baud.
   Serial1: TX=D18 -> Uno D10; RX=D19 <- Uno D11.
   Serial3: TX=D14 -> Uno D10; RX=D15 <- Uno D11. Common GND.
   Receiver sketches must parse SW=0/1 and SAMPLE=0/1 lines (see protocol).
   Fan animation lasts 6 seconds; physical fans retain their 30-second cycle.
   Battery time is a rough estimate from voltage, nominal capacity and load.
   Requires INA219 to measure ALL battery loads; not reliable while charging.
   Frame assets are adapted from the approved saved air-sample preview.
*/
